================================================================================
Video codec functionality
================================================================================

Headset and viewer video uses Pillow JPEG encoding over HTTPS/MJPEG.
The project does not declare or install aiortc or PyAV (av). The copied
framework retains unused WebRTC source modules; they are not part of the
product's supported transport or dependency set.

MP4 replay output passes raw RGB frames over a pipe to a separate host
FFmpeg subprocess configured with libx264. It does not use PyAV.
H.264 software encoding: x264, GPL-2.0-or-later (commercial licensing is
separately offered by its owner).
    https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html
    https://x264.org/licensing/

The optional OpenCV benchmark writer requests MPEG-4 Part 2 (mp4v).
Its FFmpeg build and bundled component licenses are described below.
JPEG/MJPEG: Pillow is MIT-CMU; native JPEG component notices are reproduced
in LICENSES/MIT-CMU.txt and retained in Pillow's own distribution.

opencv-python-headless 4.13.0.92, inspected manylinux x86_64 wheel:
    OpenCV is Apache-2.0. Its bundled libavcodec 62.11.100 reports
    "LGPL version 2.1 or later". The wheel's LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.txt includes
    the FFmpeg LGPL notice and libvpx's BSD terms. Other bundled libraries
    retain their own notices. This build does not enable x264/x265.
    https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python/blob/4.x/LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.txt

The retained, unused framework NVENC implementation references PyNvVideoCodec,
which is not a declared or locked dependency and is not used by the product.
That implementation requests H.264. PyNvVideoCodec 2.1.0 is MIT-licensed; Video Codec SDK and NVIDIA
driver/runtime terms remain separate. No version is pinned by this project.
    https://pypi.org/project/pynvvideocodec/2.1.0/
    https://developer.nvidia.com/pynvvideocodec

The wheel inspection covers the named Linux x86_64 builds; other platform
artifacts and the separately installed host FFmpeg require their own
build-specific license checks.

